:"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"community scores, indicating their level of satisfaction as it compares to typical people. The","bbox":[91.0394,247.99246,534.87848,258.99246],"origin":[91.0394,256.49194],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"average person (50th percentile) scores in the “Slightly Satisfied” range, while most people in","bbox":[91.0394,260.09244,543.44745,271.09244],"origin":[91.0394,268.59192],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"mental health settings score in the “Slightly Dissatisfied” category. For example, in a pooled","bbox":[91.0394,272.19241,535.49451,283.19241],"origin":[91.0394,280.69189],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"sample (n=12,234) of clients in mental health settings had a mean score of 17.04, SD=7.44","bbox":[91.0394,284.29239,534.32849,295.29239],"origin":[91.0394,292.79187],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"(Arrindell et al., 2001; Friedman, 1991; NovoPsych, 2024).","bbox":[91.0394,296.39236,374.71838,307.39236],"origin":[91.0394,304.89185],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Changes greater than half a standard deviation (3 points) are considered meaningful,","bbox":[91.0394,320.59238,504.9693,331.59238],"origin":[91.0394,329.09186],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"suggesting an improvement / deterioration in overall life satisfaction, based on a Minimally","bbox":[91.0394,332.69238,528.15735,343.69238],"origin":[91.0394,341.19186],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Importance Difference calculation (MID). The SWLS is sensitive to detecting changes in life","bbox":[91.0394,344.79239,534.26245,355.79239],"origin":[91.0394,353.29187],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"satisfaction during the course of therapy in both improvement and deterioration (Pavot & Diner,","bbox":[91.0394,356.8924,552.0274,367.8924],"origin":[91.0394,365.39188],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"2009). The scale can be complemented by the use of emotional-wellbeing and psychopathology","bbox":[91.0394,368.9924,557.5495,379.9924],"origin":[91.0394,377.49188],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"scales (Diener, 2009, pg101). Successful changes in therapy are observed with increases in","bbox":[91.0394,381.09241,539.17938,392.09241],"origin":[91.0394,389.59189],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"SWLS scores.","bbox":[91.0394,393.19241,160.72438,404.19241],"origin":[91.0394,401.69189],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Client Responses","bbox":[34.3464,420.6228,151.8204,434.6228],"origin":[34.3464,431.44031],"font":"Helvetica-Bold","size":14.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Strongly","bbox":[263.62341,444.09055,294.80145,452.59055],"origin":[263.62341,450.65833],"font":"Helvetica","size":8.5,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"agree","bbox":[268.34528,453.44055,290.07983,461.94055],"origin":[268.34528,460.00833],"font":"Helvetica","size":8.5,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Agree","bbox":[310.39328,448.76556,333.07132,457.26556],"origin":[310.39328,455.33334],"font":"Helvetica","size":8.5,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Slightly","bbox":[350.55417,444.09058,377.94968,452.59058],"origin":[350.55417,450.65836],"font":"Helvetica","size":8.5,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"agree","bbox":[353.38464,453.44058,375.1192,461.94058],"origin":[353.38464,460.00836],"font":"Helvetica","size":8.5,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Neit